{
  "_readme": [
    "The tail of the category vocabulary, classified by hand rather than by a",
    "rule. seed-taxonomy.ts handles the head deterministically; these are the",
    "strings no keyword rule could place without guessing.",
    "",
    "Two constraints held while writing this:",
    "  1. Reuse the existing l2 vocabulary. A near-duplicate l2 fragments the",
    "     taxonomy into competing SEO pages for the same intent.",
    "  2. Only two new l2 values were added, both because nothing existing was",
    "     honest: 'General Retail' for genuinely generic shop listings, and",
    "     'Musical Instruments'. Each new l2 generates a new browse page, so the",
    "     count is deliberately small.",
    "",
    "Deliberately NOT mapped: 'Bus stop', 'Apartment building' and similar.",
    "They are infrastructure or dwellings, not businesses, and the project",
    "indexes business listings only. Leaving them unmapped keeps them off the",
    "browse pages."
  ],

